WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.419
The lab runs the guide's Step 5 and
Step 6 checks in a test subscription

2
00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:09.325
where someone has applied those steps to
a test application and a pilot spoke.

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:10.887
The authors haven't run it.

4
00:00:10.887 --> 00:00:13.075
One part writes, and it's labeled.

5
00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:16.205
Step one calls the origin's
own host name directly,

6
00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:18.800
then the same request through Front Door.

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.814
The guide's Validate step says
the direct request is refused,

8
00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:27.150
a four oh three or no route, and
the one through Front Door succeeds.

9
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.314
Step two exports the
origin's access restriction:

10
00:00:30.314 --> 00:00:33.400
look for the service tag
and the header together.

11
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.262
Step three checks the
application gateway's TLS policy,

12
00:00:37.262 --> 00:00:39.613
the predefined one the guide sets.

13
00:00:39.613 --> 00:00:44.620
Step four is the failover test, and it
writes, so use only the test application:

14
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.800
stop the second origin
and call Front Door again.

15
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.125
The application should stay
available through the other origin.

16
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:53.760
Step five starts the stopped origin again.
